# ===========================================================================
# 11-scatole/Contenitore.lxqt — THE LXQt BOX, for the safety net
# ===========================================================================
#
# ⛔ This is NOT the box used to COMPILE (that one is `src/Contenitore`).
#    This is the box in which the product RUNS, with a real desktop inside.
#
# ⭐ It serves step 0 of phase 11: answering the question that blocks everything —
#    *inside a container, does the piece of the system that keeps track of who is
#    logged in behave as on the real machine?*
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⛔ R2 (§3.2 of the phase document): VERSIONS ARE DECLARED.
#    «the latest available» is a date disguised as a version.  Here the base is
#    pinned to the digest, not to the branch name.
#
#    debian:13 (trixie) — the same distribution as the test machine, and
#    not for convenience: if the box had a different distribution, a
#    worse number would say «it is the desktop» when instead it is «it is another
#    Debian».
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FROM docker.io/library/debian:13

ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. THE SYSTEM — ⛔ it is the piece step 0 must put to the test
#
#    `systemd` as the first process, `dbus`, and `dbus-user-session` without which the
#    user session has no bus of its own.  If these three do not hold in
#    here, the box does not represent the product and it must be said (§3.5).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        systemd systemd-sysv dbus dbus-user-session \
        libpam-systemd sudo procps iproute2 ca-certificates \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. THE DESKTOP — LXQt, and the same thing said for XFCE holds
#
# ⚠⚠ ⛔ **THIS BOX DOES NOT TEST A FOURTH COMPOSITOR**, and it must be
#    written here instead of letting it be discovered by reading the results: LXQt, like
#    XFCE, leans on `wlroots`, and the compositor is the SAME — `labwc`.
#    `PIANO.md` phase 13: *«the third and fourth desktops, which share wlroots
#    and therefore almost everything»*.
#
# ⇒ What this box really tests is a **fourth session**
#   and a **fourth recipe**: different packages, different dependencies, and an
#   idle daemon that `DECISIONI.md` already gives as DIFFERENT from the
#   XFCE one (`enableIdlenessWatcher` rewritten to `true` at first start).
#   ⭐ Whoever counts the results should count three compositors and four boxes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        labwc lxqt-session xwayland \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. THE GRAPHICS CARD — the software, not the iron: the iron is the real one,
#    passed inside with `--device /dev/dri`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⛔⛔ AND THE PACKAGES ARE THOSE THE REAL MACHINE HAS, not the «right» ones.
#    `[M]` 25 August 2026: on the host there are `va-driver-all 2.22.0-3` and
#    `mesa-va-drivers 25.0.7-2+deb13u1`, and ⛔ **`intel-media-va-driver-non-free`
#    is NOT there**.  The first draft of this recipe asked for it — that is, it would have
#    built a box with an encoder different from the one measured, and
#    every number would have come out incomparable.  ⇒ It is rule R2 applied
#    to a package instead of a version.
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        mesa-va-drivers va-driver-all \
        vainfo libva-drm2 libva2 libdrm2 \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. THE TEST TOOLS — few, and each with its own job
#
#   `wayland-utils`  ⭐ gives `wayland-info`, which lists what the compositor
#                    ANNOUNCES.  ⛔ It is the exact yardstick of the 25 August fault:
#                    the session that is born without any `wl_output`.
#   `weston`         gives the minimal clients (`weston-simple-shm`, `weston-terminal`):
#                    they serve the test «a window opens», ⛔ which must be
#                    looked at in the PIXEL, not in the count of processes.
#   `pipewire`       the capture path.
#   `python3-aioquic` ⛔ THE TEST CLIENT, which is the SECOND READER of the
#                    protocol (`PIANO.md` §1.1) — the only thing able to
#                    notice that server and page share the same
#                    misunderstanding.  Without it, no mesh of the net can
#                    attach to a session.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        wayland-utils weston \
        pipewire pipewire-pulse wireplumber \
        python3 python3-aioquic \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4-bis. ⛔⛔ THE LIBRARIES THE PRODUCT ASKS FOR — declared, not inherited
#
# `[M]` 26 August 2026, and it is worth writing down: without this block the
# box worked anyway, because `gnome-shell` drags along almost
# everything the product needs.  ⛔ «Almost»: `libei1` was missing, and the server
# did not start.
#
# ⚠ But the real defect was not the missing package: it was that **the others
#   were there by chance**.  The day GNOME changes a dependency, the
#   box stops having a library nobody had ever asked it for —
#   and the fault arrives months later, in a phase that has nothing to do with it.
# ⇒ They are those of the `Makefile`, line by line.  ⛔ `libngtcp2` and `libnghttp3`
#   are NOT here: those are built and copied inside with the product
#   (`11-accendi.sh prodotto`), because they are not in Debian.
# ⭐ Phase 19 (1 Oct 2026, `DECISIONI.md` §10.27): `libvulkan1` (the loader the
#   binary links) and `mesa-vulkan-drivers` (Mesa's ICDs: RADV for the
#   Radeon — the Vulkan Video road, tried BEFORE VA-API; ANV for the Intel,
#   which does not encode in Vulkan and stays on VA-API).  ⛔ Without the ICD the product
#   does not see Vulkan and falls back to VA-API saying so: the anti-regression net
#   «Radeon = Vulkan» would measure VA-API with the wrong label.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        libglib2.0-0 libpipewire-0.3-0 libdrm2 \
        libopus0 libva-drm2 \
        libvulkan1 mesa-vulkan-drivers \
        libei1 libxkbcommon0 libpam0g libssl3 \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4-ter. ⛔⛔ THE TOOLS OF **C8**, the most important mesh of the list
#
# ⭐ C8 is *«the SECOND user opens the browser»*, and the answer must be given by
#    **the pixel**: the browser renders a page, yes or no.  ⇒ To answer
#    four things are needed, and each has its own job:
#
#   `firefox-esr`     ⛔ THE REAL BROWSER, and not just any program.  The
#                     defect of 25 August 2026 is Firefox's and nobody
#                     else's: it keeps the local profile under `$HOME/.cache/mozilla`,
#                     and with a shared `~/.cache` the first user takes it with
#                     mode 0700.  ⇒ Testing with another program would mean
#                     testing another thing.
#   `ffmpeg`          the frames taken from the wire become an image.  ⚠ The
#                     LIBRARIES were already there (§4-bis); the PROGRAM was not, and they are
#                     two different things.
#   `python3-numpy`   the image judge of `10-f1-testimone.py`, which is
#   `python3-pil`     already calibrated on the real thing and ⛔ is not rewritten here.  Without them,
#                     C8 exits «I could not look» instead of falling back on a
#                     poorer judgement without saying so.
#   `fonts-dejavu-core` ⚠ without a single font Firefox draws the page
#                     anyway, ⛔ but the text becomes rectangles — and the target
#                     page has text ON PURPOSE, so as not to be «flat
#                     colour» to the judge's eyes.
#   `libpci3`         ⛔⛔ AND THIS IS THE THESIS OF THE PHASE FOR THE THIRD TIME.
#                     `[M]` 26 August 2026: without it, Firefox says `glxtest: libpci
#                     missing` and **produces no image at all** — test A
#                     gave RED to everyone, with the cure and without.
#                     ⚠ And in the XFCE box the defect did NOT show:
#                     `labwc` drags along `libpci3`, `kwin-wayland` does not.
#                     ⇒ The very same way of going wrong as `libei1` (§4-bis):
#                     a library that was there **by chance**, and a red that
#                     looked like the product's.
#
# ⚠ And the price is declared: this block makes every box grow by several
#   hundred megabytes.  ⭐ It is in ALL FOUR the same, and not only in
#   the GNOME one: if the recipes diverged, the comparison between desktops
#   would be worth less — which is the fault the user named first (D5) and
#   that C11 goes looking for.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⭐ phase 18 (1 Oct 2026): `firefox-esr` NOT from the repository but from the HOST's .deb
#   (`pacchetti/`, which `11-accendi.sh costruisci` takes from
#   /media/REMOTIX/cache/apt-host).  `[M]` 30 Sep: the trixie security repository
#   moved to 153.4.0esr while the host, and the boxes of ALL the
#   measurements of phases 15-18, have 140.16.0esr — it is rule R2 (§3): the
#   box has the packages of the real machine, not the «right» ones.
#   `apt-mark hold` so that an upgrade inside the box does not change it
#   silently.  ⚠ The version is written here on purpose: when the host changes
#   Firefox, this line changes, and it is known.
COPY pacchetti/firefox-esr_140.16.0esr-1~deb13u1_amd64.deb /tmp/pacchetti/firefox-esr.deb
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        /tmp/pacchetti/firefox-esr.deb ffmpeg \
        python3-numpy python3-pil \
        fonts-dejavu-core libpci3 \
    && apt-mark hold firefox-esr \
    && rm -rf /tmp/pacchetti /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. THE TENANT — the FIRST, and with the `render` group without which the compositor
#    would draw in software.
#
# ⚠ «the first» and not «the only»: D2 was CORRECTED by the user on 26 August
#   2026 — *«as far as I am concerned a container can even have 10 tenants,
#   it is a fact already measured with GNOME»* (`DECISIONI.md` §4.6-terdecies).
#   ⇒ The others are created by the test that needs them (C8 wants two), not by the
#     recipe: here there is only the one step 0 needs.
#
# ⚠ `provanic` and not `prova`: the name says which bench it belongs to, so that a
#   cleanup cannot step on another's toes (phase 10, §7.3).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⛔⛔ AND THE TWO GROUPS ARE CREATED IF THEY ARE NOT THERE — `[M]` 26 August 2026.
#     In the GNOME box `render` already existed: a package
#     that `gnome-shell` drags along brought it.  ⛔ In the PLASMA box **it does not
#     exist**, and the recipe died with `usermod: group 'render' does not exist`.
# ⭐⭐ And it is the thesis of this phase in miniature, happening at the first attempt:
#     **the second desktop immediately showed something the first kept
#     hidden, and not because it was broken — because it was generous.**
RUN groupadd -f video \
    && groupadd -f render \
    && useradd -u 4011 -m -s /bin/bash provanic \
    && usermod -aG video,render provanic \
    && printf 'provanic:provanic2026\n' | chpasswd

# ⛔ And the `~/.cache` must be ITS OWN.  On the test machine it is a link
#    to `/tmp` by the owner's choice (`DECISIONI.md` §4.6-undecies), and in
#    here it is not — ⚠ so this line is not needed today, and it is there anyway:
#    the box must create the tenant as the PRODUCT creates it, or the test
#    would test something easier than the real one.
RUN rm -f /home/provanic/.cache \
    && install -d -o provanic -g provanic -m 700 /home/provanic/.cache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. ⛔⛔ THE GRAPHICS CARD GROUP IS ALIGNED TO THE HOST'S
#
# `[M]` 25 August 2026, first run of step 0 — ⭐ and neither of the two
# reviewers had foreseen it.
#
# The node `/dev/dri/renderD128` enters the box with the group NUMBER it
# has on the host (991), ⛔ but inside Debian that number belongs to another
# group (`polkitd`), and the box's `render` group has another one.
# ⇒ Result of the first run: `root:polkitd 660`, the tenant left out, and
#   `[M]` **the compositor falling back on «surfaceless renderer without GPU»** —
#   that is ⛔ **a box that measures SOFTWARE encoding believing it is
#   measuring the hardware.**  No red anywhere: only worse numbers.
#
# ⚠ And the number is NOT pinned here: it is READ from the node at startup.  Pinning
#   991 would mean a box that works on this machine and stays silent on
#   another — and silence is precisely what this phase fights.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⛔⛔ 6-BIS. AND THE FILES MUST FOLLOW THE GROUP — `[M]` 27 August 2026
#
# ⭐⭐ THIS CURE IS THE CURE OF A DAMAGE WE HAD DONE TO OURSELVES, and it is worth
#     writing it in full because it is the most expensive way of going wrong
#     of the phase: **the repair of one fault opened another, in a
#     place that had nothing to do with it, and the second looked like the product's.**
#
# `groupmod -g` moves the group NUMBER, ⛔ and does NOT touch the files that already
# carry that number.  ⇒ Above, the `polkitd` group is
# moved from 991 to 1991 to make room for `render`, and from that moment:
#   `[M]` `/etc/polkit-1/rules.d` stays `root:991 drwxr-x---`, that is it passes
#   **to the `render` group**, while `polkitd` runs with group 1991 ⇒ ⛔ **it can
#   no longer read its rules directory and dies with `status=1`**,
#   silently, without a line of explanation.
#
# ⛔ And the bill for that silence: `upower.service` dies behind `polkit`
#    (**1 213 restarts**), `gnome-shell` calls them SYNCHRONOUSLY at startup and
#    takes **four 25 000 ms timeouts in a row** ⇒ for **~97 seconds
#    Mutter answers nothing**, neither D-Bus nor Wayland.
# ⇒ ⭐⭐ **The session was not born blind: it was born ~97 s late** — and
#   five meshes of the net (C2, C3, C4, C6, C8b) showed as «blocked» by a
#   defect of the BOX disguised as a defect of the PRODUCT.
#
# ⇒ The cure is HERE and not elsewhere: whoever moves the number brings the files along.
#   ⚠ `find / -xdev` and not `find /`: `/dev` is a separate mount, and the node
#     `/dev/dri/renderD128` must keep the HOST's group 991 — that is the whole
#     point of this block.
# ⛔ And it was NOT cured by widening `polkit`'s permissions nor by removing pieces
#    from its unit: that would have been a chain different from the one
#    delivered, that is a sham (§3.5).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN printf '%s\n' \
    '#!/bin/sh' \
    '# Aligns the box render group to the one of the host NODE.' \
    'set -eu' \
    'N=/dev/dri/renderD128' \
    '[ -e "$N" ] || { echo "rete11: $N is not there, the card did not get in"; exit 0; }' \
    'G=$(stat -c %g "$N")' \
    'A=$(getent group "$G" | cut -d: -f1 || true)' \
    'if [ "$A" = render ]; then echo "rete11: render is already $G"; else' \
    '  if [ -n "$A" ]; then' \
    '    groupmod -g "1$G" "$A" || true' \
    '    find / -xdev -gid "$G" -exec chgrp "1$G" {} + 2>/dev/null || true' \
    '    echo "rete11: the files of group $A followed the group to 1$G"' \
    '  fi' \
    '  groupmod -g "$G" render 2>/dev/null || groupadd -g "$G" render' \
    '  echo "rete11: render aligned to $G (it belonged to ${A:-nobody})"' \
    'fi' \
    'usermod -aG render,video provanic' \
    'id provanic' \
    > /usr/local/sbin/rete11-allinea-gruppi && chmod 755 /usr/local/sbin/rete11-allinea-gruppi

# ⛔⛔ AND THE ORDER IS PART OF THE CURE — `[M]` 27 August 2026, seen in the journal:
#     `polkit.service` started at `05:52:38.134`, died at `.199`, and the `chgrp`
#     arrived at `.296`.  ⇒ ⭐ **Ninety-seven milliseconds late, and
#     the box was born `degraded` with a dead service** — then `gnome-shell`
#     revived it from the bus and everything worked, but the red stayed written.
# ⇒ `Before=basic.target` puts THIS unit before ALL the normal services,
#   not only before `logind`: whoever moves the group numbers must have finished
#   before anyone tries to read a file carrying those numbers.
RUN printf '%s\n' \
    '[Unit]' \
    'Description=rete11 — aligns the graphics card group to the host one' \
    'Before=systemd-logind.service' \
    'Before=basic.target' \
    'Before=polkit.service' \
    'DefaultDependencies=no' \
    'After=sysinit.target' \
    '[Service]' \
    'Type=oneshot' \
    'RemainAfterExit=yes' \
    'ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/rete11-allinea-gruppi' \
    '[Install]' \
    'WantedBy=sysinit.target' \
    > /etc/systemd/system/rete11-gruppi.service \
    && systemctl enable rete11-gruppi.service

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6-bis. ⭐⭐ THE ADAPTER OF THIS DESKTOP, at the same path as all the others
#
# ⛔ It is the answer to the hardest question of the phase: the list of tests
#    is ONE and does not know which desktop it has in front of it; every box brings here its own
#    «how it is started and how it is watched».  ⇒ `fasi/11…` §3.7.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
COPY adattatore.lxqt.sh /usr/local/lib/rete11/adattatore.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. THE FIRST PROCESS — `systemd`, and it is the point of the whole box.
#
# ⛔ A container that started the desktop directly would not answer the
#    question of step 0: it would answer a more convenient one.
#
# ⚠⚠ AND THE BOX WANTS TWO EXTRA PERMISSIONS, which are NOT a detail:
#     `--cap-add=AUDIT_WRITE --cap-add=AUDIT_CONTROL`.
#     `[M]` Without the second, `pam_loginuid.so` — which in Debian's PAM chain
#     is `required` — fails with *«Cannot make/remove an entry for the
#     specified session»*, ⛔ and **the user manager does not start at all**: no
#     session, no bus, no desktop.
#     ⭐ The road chosen is to GIVE the permission, not to remove `pam_loginuid` from the
#     chain: removing it would test a PAM chain different from the one
#     delivered, that is it would test a sham (§3.5).
#     ⇒ The permissions are in `11-accendi.sh`, declared line by line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⭐ R1 — 21 September 2026, phase 13: THE CLIPBOARD ARBITERS, as on gnome
#   and kde.  `wl-clipboard` (`wl-copy`, `wl-paste`) and `python3-gi`+GTK4 (for
#   `appunti-gtk.py`) are the tools with which C17 looks at the clipboard INSIDE
#   the session.  ⛔ They belong to the BENCH, not to the product: REMOTIX does not use them.
# ⛔ Without them, C17 on this box could not look — and until 21 Sep it
#   said so with the wrong colour: RED instead of 3 (`fasi/13-xfce.md`, «The
#   bench», point 5).  ⚠ Put here even though the product does not yet
#   recognise LXQt: the box is prepared
#   BEFORE, like the real machine, not on the day it is needed.
# ⭐ And C11 looks at them (`11-c11-allineamento.py`, `DEVE_COMBACIARE`): same
#   version in all four boxes.
# ⚠ Last layer on purpose: the layers above stay as they were.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        wl-clipboard \
        python3-gi gir1.2-gtk-4.0 \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⭐ R2 — 24 September 2026, phase 14: THE REAL DESKTOP, mirroring xfce's R6.
#
# ⛔ `[R]` Until today §2 installed only `labwc lxqt-session xwayland`, and
#    with `--no-install-recommends` ⇒ **there was no LXQt desktop
#    in the box**: no panel, no file manager, no terminal, and
#    no `qt6-wayland` — that is Qt programs could not even open
#    a Wayland window.  A session like that is a compositor with nothing
#    inside, and the panel's birth faults could not be seen.
#
# ⭐ What comes in (versions `[R]` of trixie, packages.debian.org /
#   qa.debian.org/madison, 24 Sep 2026):
#   `lxqt-core` 33.2          the metapackage: in its Depends it pulls in
#                             `lxqt-panel` 2.1.4-1, `pcmanfm-qt` 2.1.0-2,
#                             `qterminal` 2.1.0-1, `lxqt-session` 2.1.1-1,
#                             `lxqt-config` 2.1.1-1, `lxqt-qtplugin` 2.1.0-1+b1,
#                             `lxqt-themes` 2.1.0-1, `lxqt-globalkeys` 2.1.0-2,
#                             `lxqt-notificationd` 2.1.1-1, `lxqt-policykit`
#                             2.1.0-1, `lxqt-runner` 2.1.2-1, `lxqt-system-theme`
#                             2.1.0-1, `qtxdg-tools`, `desktop-file-utils`.
#   `qt6-wayland` 6.8.2-4     ⛔ without it, every Qt 6 program falls back on XWayland
#                             or does not start: it is Qt's Wayland platform.
#   `lxqt-menu-data` 2.1.0-1  the `.menu` menus of the panel and of pcmanfm-qt.
#   `lxqt-powermanagement` 2.1.0-2  it is THE idle daemon of LXQt, the one
#                             `DECISIONI.md` gives as different from XFCE: without it,
#                             the box would not see the real behaviour.
#                             ⚠ It drags along `upower` (and `polkit`): the cure
#                             of §6-bis is already above, but it must be watched.
#   `nano`                    as on xfce, for manual tests.
#
# ⛔⛔ And what does NOT come in, ON PURPOSE (they are Recommends of `lxqt-core` or of
#     `lxqt-session`; `--no-install-recommends` leaves them out, and here we
#     write WHY, so that nobody puts them back «for completeness»):
#   ⛔ `lxqt-branding-debian`  puts `lxqt-leave` in the panel's quick
#                             launch: a button that closes the session
#                             within reach of a test's wrong click.
#   ⛔ `qlipper`              puts the last item back on the clipboard when
#                             it is emptied: ⇒ **it would dirty C17**, which must
#                             see on the clipboard ONLY what it puts there itself.
#   ⛔ `swayidle` `swaylock` `wlopm` `kanshi`  are the wlroots tools for
#                             idleness, locking, power-off and layout
#                             of the screens: each would change by itself the
#                             state of the session (screen locked or off,
#                             outputs shuffled) under a mesh that measures.
#                             And they are not LXQt's: LXQt has `lxqt-powermanagement`.
#
# ⚠ Last layer on purpose (before the tenant): the layers above stay
#   as they were, and the image cache is not thrown away.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        lxqt-core qt6-wayland \
        lxqt-menu-data lxqt-powermanagement \
        nano \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⭐ R3 — THE USER'S TENANT, identical to the one of `Contenitore.xfce`.
#   21 Sep 2026, asked by the user before LXQt: *«so as not to go crazy with
#   user names and passwords create in the containers the user nictest:nictest and
#   put it in the sudo group»*.  It is for HIS manual tests (Firefox,
#   terminal, file manager are already in the layers above).
# ⚠ `video` and `render` like `provanic`: without them, the session does not open the card.
# ⛔ No mesh uses it: the meshes create their own tenants (`c1u…`, `c17u…`),
#   so the user's tests and the net do not step on each other's toes.
# ⚠ Last layer on purpose: the layers above stay as they were.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN useradd -m -s /bin/bash nictest \
    && usermod -aG sudo,video,render nictest \
    && printf 'nictest:nictest\n' | chpasswd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⭐ R4 — 24 Sep 2026, phase 14: born as a DIAGNOSTIC LAYER, and since increment 3
#   ⛔ PRODUCT DEPENDENCY on LXQt: `avvia()` (src/sessione.c,
#   `primario_lxqt()`) brings `lxqt-session` to life AFTER a `wlr-randr
#   --custom-mode` at the client's size — without it, the pcmanfm-qt wallpaper
#   can stay 1280x720 with the rest black (~1 birth in 13).  ⚠ If it is missing, the
#   session is born anyway (`;`, not `&&`) and the old race comes back.
#   `wlr-randr` 0.4.1-1   `[R]` trixie: lists and changes the outputs via
#                         `zwlr_output_manager_v1` — that is it says what labwc
#                         ANNOUNCES as screens, not what we think.
#   ⚠ `wayland-utils` (`wayland-info`) is NOT repeated here: it is already in §4,
#     in all four boxes.  ⚠ `lswt` does NOT exist in Debian
#     (no version on qa.debian.org, 24 Sep 2026).
# ⚠ C11 (`11-c11-allineamento.py`) compares only its DEVE_COMBACIARE list,
#   and `wlr-randr` is not in it: one extra package only here does not turn it red.
# ⚠ Last layer on purpose: the layers above stay as they were.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        wlr-randr \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⭐ R5 — 24 Sep 2026, phase 14, increment 2: THE PANEL ICONS.
# [M] With R2..R4 the LXQt panel was born WITHOUT icons and WITHOUT the menu
#     button: a row of empty spaces.
# ⭐ What comes in, and why `[R]`:
#   `kf6-breeze-icon-theme`  the icon theme LXQt expects:
#                            lxqt-session 2.1.1, `config/lxqt.conf:3`
#                            `icon_theme=breeze`.  It would be brought by
#                            `lxqt-system-theme`, but ONLY as Recommends
#                            (papirus | breeze | faenza | oxygen) ⇒
#                            `--no-install-recommends` discards it.
#   `qt6-svg-plugins`        the menu button takes its icon from the theme's
#                            qss: lxqt-themes 2.1.0,
#                            `system/lxqt-panel.qss:72`
#                            `qproperty-icon: url(mainmenu.svg)`; and Qt 6 loads such an
#                            `.svg` only with the SVG image
#                            plugin.  The breeze icons are svg too.
# ⚠⚠ It is the BOX, not the product: a real machine with normal `apt`
#    takes the Recommends and already has these two things.  Here they are put back by
#    hand so that the box resembles the real machine: the box is
#    prepared like the real machine.
# [?] Exact trixie versions to be read in the box (`dpkg -l`): not
#     looked up on qa.debian.org for this layer.
# ⚠ NEW layer at the end, on purpose, instead of lengthening R2's line:
#   touching R2 would throw away the cache of R2, R3 and R4 (three layers, one with the
#   whole desktop) for two packages that depend on none of them.
#   Down here R1..R4 stay identical and only this one is rebuilt.
# ⚠ C11 (`DEVE_COMBACIARE`) does not list them: one extra package only here
#   does not turn it red.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        kf6-breeze-icon-theme qt6-svg-plugins \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

STOPSIGNAL SIGRTMIN+3
CMD ["/sbin/init"]
